# SRG-APP-000173-AU-002560  -  CAT III
# The Central Log Server must be configured to enforce 24 hours/1 day as the
# minimum password lifetime.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations, then kept
# by hand. Edit this file to change how this requirement is assessed here;
# it is read at run time. Regenerating refreshes the benchmark text in place
# and leaves the criteria, the determination and any verification block as
# they are.

id:              SRG-APP-000173-AU-002560
group:           V-206476
severity:        low
cat:             CAT III
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       manual
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-004066
control_rev5:    IA-5

contribution:    The product can only limit reuse, not frequency: enablePasswordHistory
                 with passwordHistoryCount stops a user returning to a stored previous
                 password, and authType can delegate native authentication to a provider
                 that does enforce a minimum age.

external:        An external authentication provider selected through authentication.conf
                 authType (LDAP, SAML or Scripted), whose policy engine can enforce a
                 24-hour minimum password lifetime
external:        The organization's password management procedure for the native emergency
                 account of last resort
external:        Operating system password aging for host accounts

manual_reason:   Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 has no minimum password age or minimum password
                 lifetime setting. The complete set of native password controls at
                 authentication.conf.spec:437-568 covers minimum length, character-class
                 minimums, expiry in days, expiry alerting, lockout, and password history;
                 none of them prevents a password from being changed again inside 24 hours,
                 so no configuration value can decide this requirement and a condition over
                 password history would report a finding for a control the product does not
                 implement.

citation:        SRG-APP-000173-AU-002560 check text; authentication.conf.spec:437-568
                 (full [splunk_auth] control set; expirePasswordDays at 487-494 is a
                 maximum lifetime, not a minimum; enablePasswordHistory at 554-560 and
                 passwordHistoryCount at 561-568), authentication.conf.spec:30-33 (authType
                 vocabulary)
finding:         Not a finding against the application: Splunk Enterprise 10.4.2 provides
                 no minimum password lifetime or minimum password age setting, and the
                 24-hour floor is carried by the external authentication provider or by
                 organizational password procedure.
